WEBVTT

00:10.640 --> 00:12.040
Depth 100 meters.

00:12.840 --> 00:14.280
Battery check.

00:14.940 --> 00:16.980
Oxygen partial pressure check.

00:16.980 --> 00:20.180
No abnormalities in any section.
Operation normal!

00:22.020 --> 00:24.250
What happened to the live broadcast, Eri?

00:27.160 --> 00:28.350
I'm tired of it.

00:29.990 --> 00:31.260
She's asleep.

00:35.300 --> 00:36.270
What is it?

00:38.200 --> 00:40.240
Karen is so lucky.

00:40.240 --> 00:42.210
She can eat that much and not get fat.

00:42.940 --> 00:45.610
I wonder if all the nutrients end up in her breasts?

00:45.610 --> 00:47.670
Hey, what do you think, Aika?

00:49.610 --> 00:51.050
Who cares about that?

00:51.050 --> 00:53.380
Sit in your seat properly, it's going to shake.

00:55.420 --> 00:56.620
See! Here it comes!

00:56.620 --> 00:58.550
What? What's going on?

00:58.550 --> 01:02.120
Looks like we smashed into the stagnation of the middle layer current.

01:02.120 --> 01:03.790
It'll be okay, right?

01:03.790 --> 01:05.190
Leave it to me!

01:05.190 --> 01:06.600
I'm worried because it's you!

01:06.600 --> 01:07.690
Hey!

01:27.450 --> 01:35.260
Holding the rising sun to my heart

01:35.260 --> 01:40.860
I look far into the distant sky

01:42.270 --> 01:52.260
When I closed my eyes, a nostalgic wind blew between the memories

01:56.510 --> 02:06.510
Even if your painfully shiny smile is filled with tears, I'll live on

02:14.500 --> 02:21.900
We were born into a time where we can't go back

02:21.900 --> 02:29.310
No matter what awaits in the future that quickly passes by

02:29.310 --> 02:36.650
We'll walk on by trusting the endless love

02:36.650 --> 02:44.320
And tightly holding onto my own feelings alone

02:48.330 --> 02:53.130
Deep Blue Girl

02:54.200 --> 02:56.400
The shaking's died down, but...

02:58.770 --> 03:01.010
Karen's looking kind of shaken up.

03:01.480 --> 03:02.880
There's light right ahead!

03:03.510 --> 03:04.580
What, what?

03:04.580 --> 03:07.880
See, over there, red light and white light.

03:09.490 --> 03:10.850
What is that?

03:11.320 --> 03:12.550
Beats me.

03:13.120 --> 03:14.680
I can't tell from this distance.

03:15.460 --> 03:17.480
An airport?

03:18.260 --> 03:20.060
It is!

03:20.060 --> 03:23.570
Remember the captain saying that there was once an airport?

03:23.570 --> 03:25.230
And the lights are even on...

03:25.230 --> 03:26.830
Looking good, looking good!

03:33.980 --> 03:35.780
I wonder if anyone's there.

03:35.780 --> 03:37.040
Maybe so.

03:40.880 --> 03:42.350
Who?

03:42.350 --> 03:43.350
No clue...

03:43.350 --> 03:44.490
No clue?!

03:44.490 --> 03:46.460
That's what we're here to find out.

03:46.990 --> 03:49.960
Please proceed following the green light.

03:51.190 --> 03:54.060
The green, green!
See, over there! Right there!

03:54.060 --> 03:56.260
Be quiet! I know.

03:56.900 --> 03:59.640
It looks like a secret base.

03:59.640 --> 04:03.270
I can just smell the adventure!
I can smell it!

04:03.270 --> 04:07.180
Hey, speed up! Engines to full!

04:07.180 --> 04:09.410
Shut up a second, you adventure freak.

04:13.020 --> 04:15.850
There's a hangar-like building ahead.

04:15.850 --> 04:18.340
There is an opening to the shaft inside.

04:18.850 --> 04:19.960
Go in there.

04:19.960 --> 04:21.010
Roger.

04:27.630 --> 04:30.770
Okay, we're entering the shaft!

04:30.770 --> 04:32.470
Here we go again.

04:32.470 --> 04:37.140
The word "shaft" causes your reporter to recall ancient dugout houses,

04:37.140 --> 04:40.130
but that's just the way I feel, so don't mind me.

04:41.540 --> 04:45.410
The submarine is slowly, slowly descending.

04:45.410 --> 04:49.120
We started at level one and now we are at level six.

04:49.120 --> 04:50.550
We'll keep descending!

04:50.290 --> 04:51.920
Shut up already!

04:52.460 --> 04:54.290
Measuring with sonar, directly below.

04:55.060 --> 04:56.150
20...

04:56.760 --> 04:59.250
15... The bottom's close.

05:00.030 --> 05:02.290
Descending speed, 3...

05:03.100 --> 05:04.260
2...

05:04.870 --> 05:06.200
1...

05:06.200 --> 05:07.500
Stop.

05:07.500 --> 05:09.110
We are finally at level 9.

05:09.110 --> 05:10.700
Oh, please look!

05:12.610 --> 05:14.640
The shutter is open, for some reason.

05:14.640 --> 05:16.250
It's an unknown! It's a mystery!

05:16.250 --> 05:20.280
My friendly adventure club and I must go in!

05:20.280 --> 05:22.440
Who are you calling a friendly adventure club?

05:23.190 --> 05:24.650
Inside is pitch dark!

05:24.650 --> 05:26.050
Listen.

05:27.890 --> 05:29.330
It's okay, right?

05:29.330 --> 05:30.590
Go!

05:30.590 --> 05:32.460
Not you!

05:32.460 --> 05:33.830
Dammit.

06:09.830 --> 06:12.170
All right, we're here!

06:12.170 --> 06:13.140
Let's get off.

06:13.140 --> 06:16.660
Don't rush. We'll first analyze the air and pressurize.

06:27.220 --> 06:28.880
What are you doing?! Take turns!

06:28.880 --> 06:30.350
You're too slow!

06:30.350 --> 06:31.790
Anyway, get back inside.

06:31.790 --> 06:32.820
No!

06:32.490 --> 06:33.790
No, my ass!

06:36.760 --> 06:38.790
People are waiting.

06:51.470 --> 06:52.470
Is this it?

06:52.470 --> 06:53.770
Hey!

07:01.280 --> 07:02.510
It opened.

07:06.020 --> 07:08.820
What's this? A large pathway?

07:08.820 --> 07:10.660
Come on, Karen.

07:13.100 --> 07:14.430
Hey...

07:15.130 --> 07:16.430
Wait a second!

07:17.130 --> 07:18.200
What?

07:18.200 --> 07:22.640
You're insane, just recklessly pressing buttons and going in!

07:22.640 --> 07:24.910
We don't know what kind of place this is!

07:24.910 --> 07:26.010
It's okay.

07:26.010 --> 07:27.580
It's not okay!

07:27.580 --> 07:28.980
What if something happens?

07:28.980 --> 07:31.540
I know about this place.

07:32.450 --> 07:34.180
You know...

07:34.920 --> 07:36.020
You know?

07:36.020 --> 07:40.750
Karen's butterfly emblem also referred to this place.

07:42.630 --> 07:44.150
I didn't hear about that.

07:45.330 --> 07:46.450
I just told you.

07:47.530 --> 07:48.830
What are you doing?!

07:48.830 --> 07:51.630
Tell me everything you know!
Right now!

07:51.630 --> 07:54.900
Ow! What are you going to do if I get bruised?!

07:54.900 --> 07:56.440
Just tell me!

07:56.440 --> 07:59.140
I'll talk! This hurts!

08:01.640 --> 08:02.650
What's that sound?

08:02.650 --> 08:03.980
I don't know.

08:03.980 --> 08:05.210
Let's head back!

08:05.850 --> 08:08.020
What are you saying?
We came this far!

08:08.020 --> 08:09.420
It's too dangerous!

08:12.150 --> 08:13.350
Karen?

08:14.920 --> 08:16.480
She's going, she's going!

08:18.260 --> 08:19.350
Dammit.

08:22.560 --> 08:24.200
A few decades ago,

08:24.200 --> 08:27.900
there was an organism stuck to a crashed meteorite.

08:28.440 --> 08:33.510
That life-form was able to survive by living off humans.

08:33.510 --> 08:36.280
I've seen that kind of movie before.

08:36.280 --> 08:40.920
The human that became the host slows down in physical growth,

08:40.920 --> 08:44.090
but advances dramatically in brain function.

08:44.090 --> 08:47.290
Brain function...
They become smarter.

08:47.290 --> 08:48.760
We can see it now.

08:57.130 --> 09:00.230
The door is open a little. Someone's...

09:00.570 --> 09:01.640
Go, Aika.

09:01.640 --> 09:03.140
Why me?

09:03.140 --> 09:05.200
Because it's dangerous, of course.

09:07.480 --> 09:08.340
Go!

09:08.340 --> 09:10.070
I'm not a dog!

09:27.500 --> 09:28.620
I see.

09:29.300 --> 09:32.700
Aika, can't you recall that door's design?

09:36.470 --> 09:41.440
Yeah, the thing that was on the girls who attacked us at the beach.

09:41.440 --> 09:43.170
They were like that too.

09:44.080 --> 09:46.020
We can't ignore this connection.

09:46.020 --> 09:50.320
That should be the last gate, the gate to the truth!

09:51.220 --> 09:53.050
There you go, Karen.

09:53.520 --> 09:55.010
Is that so?

09:55.960 --> 09:57.760
Why does it end up like this?

09:57.760 --> 09:59.520
Okay, this way, Karen.

10:00.930 --> 10:02.230
Here I go!

10:07.370 --> 10:08.630
What is it?

10:09.140 --> 10:12.200
How strange.
Karen should be the key.

10:12.780 --> 10:14.380
No wonder it's a mystery.

10:14.380 --> 10:19.250
Your mind is the mystery.
The gate won't open like that!

10:19.250 --> 10:21.050
It's not that easy, is it?

10:27.190 --> 10:30.030
Hey, what are you going to do if something happens?

10:30.030 --> 10:32.360
I'm doing it so something does happen.

10:32.360 --> 10:33.450
This one.

10:37.430 --> 10:38.460
Bingo.

10:42.400 --> 10:46.930
This is it! The keyhole that will open the gate of truth!

10:49.550 --> 10:50.950
A scanner?

10:53.220 --> 10:54.580
Then, if you would...

10:55.480 --> 10:56.710
An anesthetic gun?

10:57.820 --> 10:59.080
I see.

10:59.790 --> 11:00.810
Roger.

11:01.320 --> 11:03.290
What are you going to do with that?

11:05.290 --> 11:07.500
Here I go, Karen.

11:07.500 --> 11:09.830
Eri, what are you...

11:09.830 --> 11:13.630
"The gate of truth will be opened by the sleeping butterfly."

11:16.170 --> 11:17.830
I'll leave the rest up to you.

11:26.920 --> 11:28.010
Eri...

11:30.090 --> 11:31.210
Give me a hand.

11:31.820 --> 11:32.920
With what?

11:32.920 --> 11:34.180
We're gonna undress her.

11:34.690 --> 11:35.990
Why?

11:35.990 --> 11:42.160
That scanner probably reads the body's vein pattern and other data.

11:42.760 --> 11:44.860
That's why clothes will get in the way.

11:45.270 --> 11:47.040
Are you sure?

11:47.040 --> 11:49.240
She said she'll leave the rest up to us.

11:49.240 --> 11:50.570
Come on, hurry!

11:54.780 --> 11:57.650
I don't think you had to take everything off.

11:57.650 --> 11:59.340
We have to take extra precautions.

11:59.780 --> 12:02.550
But she's got such a nice figure.

12:03.090 --> 12:05.020
I'm so jealous.

12:05.820 --> 12:07.160
Eri, are you...

12:07.160 --> 12:08.260
What?

12:08.260 --> 12:10.520
Nah, never mind.

12:11.090 --> 12:14.400
Okay, let's lay Karen on the scanner.

12:14.400 --> 12:16.760
It really is that kind of club.

12:25.610 --> 12:26.800
It's moving.

12:49.430 --> 12:50.760
It opened.

12:56.940 --> 12:58.070
Hey!

12:59.210 --> 13:01.380
We're finally here!

13:01.380 --> 13:04.180
Karen, it opened.

13:05.380 --> 13:09.650
Wow, it's spacious, big, huge!
Wow, it's huge!

13:09.650 --> 13:12.750
Wow! What's this?

13:12.750 --> 13:14.310
What's here?

13:17.630 --> 13:20.760
How is this place related to Karen?

13:20.760 --> 13:22.090
Idiot!

13:22.970 --> 13:24.990
That's what we came here to find out.

13:25.470 --> 13:26.830
Yeah, that's true.

13:27.370 --> 13:29.400
Hey, don't call me an idiot!

13:29.810 --> 13:31.040
What are you doing?

13:31.040 --> 13:34.240
I thought, "Hey, is something in there?" So I'm looking.

13:34.840 --> 13:37.010
Shouldn't you look over there?

13:42.380 --> 13:44.290
It's all numbers.

13:44.290 --> 13:46.090
It's because it's research data.

13:46.090 --> 13:47.620
I feel dizzy.

13:47.620 --> 13:50.290
You hate the sciences, don't you?

13:50.290 --> 13:51.360
How rude.

13:51.360 --> 13:54.930
Shouldn't you take a copy back and ask an expert?

13:54.930 --> 13:56.270
I'll look at it some more.

13:56.270 --> 13:58.230
That won't help.

13:59.200 --> 14:03.700
You mentioned earlier that space organisms live off of humans, right?

14:04.740 --> 14:06.510
Yeah, so?

14:06.510 --> 14:09.340
Is it possible that Karen is the host?

14:10.550 --> 14:11.750
Right?

14:11.750 --> 14:15.620
Yeah, if you're a host, then you develop significantly...

14:17.150 --> 14:20.220
That's why her boobs and butt are so nice.

14:20.220 --> 14:22.420
The thing that develops is here.

14:24.330 --> 14:25.520
Hey, a picture.

14:26.260 --> 14:28.890
It seems like it's comparing various cells,

14:29.670 --> 14:31.660
but they all look the same.

14:32.770 --> 14:34.140
A clone?

14:34.140 --> 14:37.770
Clone! Yeah, these are clone cells!

14:37.770 --> 14:41.810
They were researching cells that they cloned from the host.

14:41.810 --> 14:43.450
But why?

14:43.450 --> 14:45.550
The host's development slows.

14:45.550 --> 14:48.680
In other words, it prevents aging, right?

14:49.480 --> 14:50.790
You're right,

14:50.790 --> 14:54.160
plus the brain develops and you get smarter.

14:54.160 --> 14:58.890
If you cultivate those cells, and can use it for humans, then...

14:59.660 --> 15:01.560
It'd change the world.

15:01.560 --> 15:03.070
Even history.

15:03.070 --> 15:06.270
But that utopian pursuit was never fulfilled.

15:06.270 --> 15:08.700
It's like modern alchemy!

15:08.700 --> 15:10.570
No, it's a little different.

15:11.270 --> 15:14.780
If we have an expert look at this, then we can learn a lot.

15:14.780 --> 15:17.250
Didn't I just say that?

15:17.250 --> 15:19.740
We need to take Karen out of the scanner.

15:20.850 --> 15:22.110
Good grief...

15:23.550 --> 15:25.540
What? You sound weird.

15:34.100 --> 15:36.260
Karen?

15:36.800 --> 15:39.060
No, it's not Karen!

15:40.640 --> 15:41.830
Not to mention...

15:46.210 --> 15:49.580
Karen multiplied!

15:49.580 --> 15:51.610
No, they're clones!

15:51.610 --> 15:53.250
Clones?

15:53.250 --> 15:54.520
I see.

15:54.520 --> 15:56.250
Um, we are...

16:04.690 --> 16:06.060
They attacked!

16:06.660 --> 16:09.150
They want to get rid of us, the foreign objects.

16:11.330 --> 16:12.730
Not good.

16:12.730 --> 16:14.030
Eri, run!

16:14.640 --> 16:15.730
Hurry!

16:38.060 --> 16:39.360
Still want to?

16:46.030 --> 16:48.300
I don't know what they're saying!

16:49.100 --> 16:51.470
That's our Aika! Way to go!

16:57.050 --> 16:58.980
It's so small.

16:59.550 --> 17:01.710
Move. You're gonna get hurt.

17:05.720 --> 17:06.620
Eri!

17:31.910 --> 17:33.540
Ow!

17:51.300 --> 17:52.790
Oh yeah, Eri!

18:04.480 --> 18:07.070
Don't mess with my friend!

18:07.950 --> 18:09.040
Aika...

18:27.600 --> 18:29.590
Eri, nice!

18:31.870 --> 18:34.210
She was small, so I let my guard down.

18:36.280 --> 18:40.220
Can't let your guard down, right? I'm a little...

18:41.650 --> 18:43.620
What? What's wrong?

18:49.790 --> 18:52.320
No! No!

18:56.000 --> 18:57.060
Eri!

19:13.280 --> 19:17.090
What was that? Are you telling me that's a clone too?

19:17.090 --> 19:18.820
You gotta be kidding me!

19:32.130 --> 19:33.260
Hurry!

20:42.100 --> 20:43.370
Thank you.

20:47.680 --> 20:49.940
Aika... Aika!

20:49.940 --> 20:52.480
Wake up... Wake up...

20:52.480 --> 20:53.710
Wake up!

20:57.720 --> 20:59.050
Where's Karen?!

20:59.050 --> 21:00.040
Where are the clones?!

21:00.820 --> 21:02.190
Ouch!

21:02.590 --> 21:03.820
Well...

21:20.410 --> 21:22.340
I see...

21:23.040 --> 21:25.570
I was also made here.

21:36.690 --> 21:38.130
Let's go back.

21:47.700 --> 21:49.000
Where are they?

21:49.600 --> 21:51.970
It seems like they are going back to sleep.

22:25.110 --> 22:26.600
They're disappearing...

22:27.480 --> 22:29.170
Good night.

22:32.380 --> 22:33.950
You know, Eri,

22:33.950 --> 22:37.440
it's too bad we couldn't get a trophy for this adventure.

22:38.750 --> 22:40.020
We got one.

22:40.520 --> 22:41.790
We got what?

22:42.690 --> 22:44.560
This, this!

22:44.560 --> 22:48.460
Isn't it awesome?
A picture with the huge Karen.

22:49.530 --> 22:51.370
You were taking pictures like that...

22:51.370 --> 22:53.640
I took it.

22:53.640 --> 22:55.900
This is the leg, right?

22:55.900 --> 22:57.200
Isn't it cool?

22:57.940 --> 22:59.210
Kinda...

22:59.210 --> 23:00.900
What do you mean, kinda?

23:27.600 --> 23:30.900
It was a little close, wasn't it, Miss Salvager?

23:31.310 --> 23:33.830
I appreciate the rescue, Captain!

23:34.310 --> 23:37.470
If you died on me,
I'd be in big trouble.

23:39.380 --> 23:42.220
Captain! Are you carrying that baggage to the sick bay?

23:42.220 --> 23:47.490
Gusto! She's a rich young lady.
Watch what you're saying.

23:47.920 --> 23:50.290
Sir! Please excuse me!

24:02.800 --> 24:04.930
My memory...

24:06.740 --> 24:09.040
...wasn't the real one.

24:15.820 --> 24:17.120
Let's make them.

24:19.520 --> 24:22.980
Let's make a lot of memories together.

24:27.660 --> 24:28.890
Thank you.

24:47.520 --> 24:49.710
Was the trip fun?

24:51.050 --> 24:52.540
What are you talking about?

25:01.660 --> 25:03.760
Seems like you really had fun.

25:04.900 --> 25:07.600
I have a clear view about the decision I made.

25:09.170 --> 25:11.940
It'd be much better if you have a clear idea about what's ahead.

25:15.680 --> 25:17.750
Did you not have enough fun?

25:17.750 --> 25:22.550
Hey, how weird.
I was watching carefully.

25:24.320 --> 25:28.660
A lot happened, but my first job was a great success.

25:28.660 --> 25:32.750
I expertly salvaged Karen's smile.

25:33.330 --> 25:37.960
A bit of the mystery is still left, but I'll set that aside for now.

25:39.130 --> 25:41.690
With that, the case is closed!

25:48.910 --> 25:56.940
I swear to that dream that

25:48.910 --> 25:56.940
I will protect you, rise

26:00.620 --> 26:12.500
No one waits at the farthest end

26:00.620 --> 26:12.500
of someone else's dream

26:09.530 --> 26:11.270
Okay, you're late.

26:11.270 --> 26:13.270
Eri, come on!

26:12.500 --> 26:22.840
I wished for feelings to be carried

26:12.500 --> 26:22.840
and flown up high into the sky

26:14.840 --> 26:16.870
Oh, Karen.

26:16.870 --> 26:18.640
Good morning.

26:18.640 --> 26:21.910
Good morning. But you're late.

26:21.910 --> 26:23.410
It's only a little.

26:23.410 --> 26:25.010
That's still not okay.

26:24.210 --> 26:29.920
I was endlessly struggling

26:24.210 --> 26:29.920
and miserably in pain

26:25.010 --> 26:26.050
Demon!

26:26.050 --> 26:28.050
Call me whatever you want, you late chick.

26:28.520 --> 26:31.650
Ms. Risako, there are two people who are late today.

26:29.920 --> 26:37.460
So I tightly gripped

26:29.920 --> 26:37.460
my weakness in my hands

26:33.020 --> 26:35.790
Come to the staff room later, you two.

26:36.860 --> 26:38.760
I'll tell people about last time.

26:37.460 --> 26:49.240
I swear I'll send you the hopes

26:37.460 --> 26:49.240
that melt the sadness, rise

26:38.760 --> 26:42.430
Go ahead! No one will believe you.

26:44.830 --> 26:49.570
Karen, say something to that evil teacher.

26:49.240 --> 26:58.950
I'll head to tomorrow by holding

26:49.240 --> 26:58.950
onto niceness and strength

26:49.940 --> 26:51.870
Good morning.

26:51.870 --> 26:53.370
Good morning to you.

26:58.950 --> 27:04.810
And I'll swear, rise

26:59.810 --> 27:01.050
Oh, well...

27:01.050 --> 27:02.580
What are you talking about?
You were late!

27:02.580 --> 27:04.190
I'm not talking about that!

27:06.890 --> 27:13.060
I'll swear to tomorrow, rise

27:10.290 --> 27:23.060
Congratulations on the First Treasure
Hunting Club's Adventure - Big Success

27:28.080 --> 27:29.410
Next episode is...

27:29.410 --> 27:31.210
Is there a next episode?

27:30.710 --> 27:31.850
There isn't?

27:31.210 --> 27:32.510
I think it's the end.

27:32.510 --> 27:33.780
We did what we had to do.

27:33.780 --> 27:34.780
We have nothing to do.

27:34.780 --> 27:36.150
Wanna go out on an adventure?

27:35.480 --> 27:36.650
The treasure hunting club ended.

27:36.650 --> 27:37.720
How fast!

